-- table --
Call methods with named arguments:
  overseer.getStatus()
  let page = overseer.queryMessages(limit: 10)
  page.items | take(3)

Bindings are lazy: their first use saves the result or error, even cancellation.
Rebind to try again, or use a function for fresh calls:
  let status = () => overseer.getStatus()
  status()

_ holds the last successful result. x | f(y) means f(x, y).
nil is a missing value; null is also accepted. JSON always uses null.
A method name without parentheses shows its documentation, without calling it.
Lists are fetched in full; pipes do not stream or fetch more pages.

  :help [NAME]  help for a method, type, or function
  :schema       show the schema
  :vars         show user bindings
  :quit         exit

Save scripts as *.purl and run them with purl -f FILE ENDPOINT.
Tab completes without making calls. Ctrl-R searches history.
Long output uses $PAGER or less. NO_PAGER disables paging.
Ctrl-C cancels input or evaluation; Ctrl-D exits.
History may contain secrets. Start input with a space to exclude it,
or use -no-history to disable history entirely.

Builtins:
  FUNCTION                    DESCRIPTION
  age(timestamp)              Whole seconds since an RFC 3339 timestamp; future is negative.
  all(items, fn)              Whether all items match; stop on false.
  any(items, fn)              Whether any item matches; stop on true.
  assert(condition, message)  Return nil on true; otherwise fail with message.
  bytes(text)                 Encode a string as UTF-8 bytes.
  contains(text, part)        Case-sensitive substring match.
  count(items)                Count items, fields, bytes, or Unicode characters.
  endsWith(text, part)        Case-sensitive suffix match.
  filter(items, fn)           Keep items whose predicate is true.
  find(items, fn)             First match, or nil; stop at the first match.
  groupBy(items, fn)          Group equal keys into {key, items} records in first-seen order.
  keys(record)                List record field names.
  map(items, fn)              Apply fn to each item.
  parseJSON(text)             Parse JSON without losing integer precision.
  sortBy(items, fn)           Stable-sort items by their computed keys.
  startsWith(text, part)      Case-sensitive prefix match.
  sum(items)                  Sum numbers; empty lists yield 0.
  take(items, n)              First n items.
  text(bytes)                 Decode UTF-8 bytes into a string.
  toJSON(value)               Encode a value as JSON.
  uniqueBy(items, fn)         Keep the first item for each equal key.

Methods:
  greeter.getUser
  greeter.listUsers
  greeter.ping

